{"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLPosition","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"MXLPosition","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/init(defaultX:defaultY:relativeX:relativeY:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/defaultX","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/defaultY","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/relativeX","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/relativeY"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/Equatable-Implementations"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default-x and default-y attributes change the computation of the default position. For most elements, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"origin is changed relative to the left-hand side of the note or the musical position within the bar (x) and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the top line of the staff (y)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the following elements, the default-x value changes the origin relative to the start of the current"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measure:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"note - figured-bass - harmony - link - directive - measure-numbering - all descendants of the part-list","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element - all children of the direction-type element","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This origin is from the start of the entire measure, at either the left barline or the start of the system."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the default-x attribute is used within a child element of the part-name-display, part-abbreviation-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"display, group-name-display, or group-abbreviation-display elements, it changes the origin relative to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"start of the first measure on the system. These values are used when the current measure or a succeeding"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measure starts a new system. The same change of origin is used for the group-symbol element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the note, figured-bass, and harmony elements, the default-x value is considered to have adjusted the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"musical position within the bar for its descendant elements.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Since the credit-words and credit-image elements are not related to a measure, in these cases the default-x"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and default-y attributes adjust the origin relative to the bottom left-hand corner of the specified page."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The relative-x and relative-y attributes change the position relative to the default position, either as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"computed by the individual program, or as overridden by the default-x and default-y attributes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Positive x is right, negative x is left; positive y is up, negative y is down. All units are in tenths of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interline space. For stems, positive relative-y lengthens a stem while negative relative-y shortens it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The default-x and default-y position attributes provide higher-resolution positioning data than related","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"features such as the placement attribute and the offset element. Applications reading a MusicXML file that can","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"understand both features should generally rely on the default-x and default-y attributes for their greater"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accuracy. For the relative-x and relative-y attributes, the offset element, placement attribute, and directive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute provide context for the relative position information, so the two features should be interpreted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"together."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As elsewhere in the MusicXML format, tenths are the global tenths defined by the scaling element, not the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"local tenths of a staff resized by the staff-size element."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition/defaultX":{"abstract":[{"text":"The default horizontal position, in tenths, changing the computation of the default position relative to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left-hand side of the note or the musical position within the measure.","type":"text"}],"title":"defaultX","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/defaultX","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition\/defaultx","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"defaultX"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition":{"title":"MXLPosition","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","abstract":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"},"doc://IvorMXL/SQ":{"title":"Swift.Equatable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition/relativeY":{"title":"relativeY","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"relativeY"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition\/relativey","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertical position, in tenths, relative to the default position, either as computed by the application or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as overridden by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"defaultY"},{"type":"text","text":". Positive values are up, negative values down; for stems, a positive value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lengthens the stem while a negative value shortens it."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/relativeY"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition/init(defaultX:defaultY:relativeX:relativeY:)":{"title":"init(defaultX:defaultY:relativeX:relativeY:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"defaultX"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"defaultY"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"relativeX"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"relativeY"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?)"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition\/init(defaultx:defaulty:relativex:relativey:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLPosition"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/init(defaultX:defaultY:relativeX:relativeY:)"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition/Equatable-Implementations":{"title":"Equatable Implementations","role":"collectionGroup","type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition\/equatable-implementations","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/Equatable-Implementations"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition/defaultY":{"title":"defaultY","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"defaultY"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition\/defaulty","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/defaultY","abstract":[{"text":"The default vertical position, in tenths, changing the computation of the default position relative to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"top line of the staff.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition/relativeX":{"title":"relativeX","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"relativeX"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition\/relativex","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The horizontal position, in tenths, relative to the default position, either as computed by the application"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or as overridden by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"defaultX"},{"type":"text","text":". Positive values are to the right, negative values to the left."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/relativeX"},"doc://IvorMXL/SH":{"title":"Swift.Hashable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH"},"doc://IvorMXL/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP"},"doc://IvorMXL/s8CopyableP":{"title":"Swift.Copyable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP"},"doc://IvorMXL/s9EscapableP":{"title":"Swift.Escapable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"}}}